lid D levels.", "watch": "Fresh polling or outside spending on Hull's behalf could tighten the race, though he would need a substantial late shift to overcome the current gap.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Michelle Lujan Grisham (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Mexico's governorship is open this year with Michelle Lujan Grisham term-limited, and Democrats turn to former Interior Secretary Deb Haaland while Republicans nominate Gregg Hull. The state's D+4 lean, a favorable national environment, and a lopsided money race, in which Haaland has raised about $11.1 million to Hull's roughly $474,000, all point her way. Race raters uniformly place the contest in Democratic territory, ranging from Likely D to Safe D.\n\nIndependent polling has been sparse, with the last public survey in late August showing Haaland ahead by six points among likely voters, and averages of compiled polls putting her lead between roughly eight and eleven points. Betting markets price her chances at 94 to 95 percent. The main open question is the size of the margin rather than the winner; the unresolved debate standoff drew headlines through late September but has not visibly moved the race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 10.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9571, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9605, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.948, "margin": 10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9415, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9502, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9552, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9463, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9506, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9559, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 10.0}]}